## 2. Config-driven assist & tools setup

Create two config files under `IPRU_NexGen/config/`:

**`assistConfig.ts`**
```ts
export interface AssistConfig {
  id: string;            // e.g. "pms-assist"
  trigger: string;        // e.g. "/pms-assist"
  label: string;           // e.g. "PMS Assist"
  description: string;    // shown in dropdown
  icon?: string;
  enabled: boolean;
}
```
Seed with `pms-assist` and `pst-assist` entries (matching current functionality). Adding a third assist later should require only a new entry here — no logic changes elsewhere.

**`toolsConfig.ts`**
```ts
export interface ToolConfig {
  id: string;             // e.g. "create-doc"
  trigger: string;         // e.g. "@create-doc"
  label: string;
  description: string;
  icon?: string;
  category: "feature";     // reserved for future grouping
  enabled: boolean;
}
```
Seed with all 8 tools from the spec (`chat-with-doc`, `create-doc`, `chat-with-pdf`, `create-pdf`, `chat-with-excel`, `create-excel`, `translate-document`, `send-mail`), even though most aren't functional until later phases — `enabled: false` is fine for the ones not yet built if you want to hide them from the dropdown until their phase lands. Confirm with me before hiding any — default assumption is **show all, functionality lands later.**

Both configs should be the single source of truth the autocomplete component reads from — no hardcoded lists in the component itself.

