## 4. Trigger autocomplete component

Build a new `TriggerAutocomplete` component, anchored to and sliding in above the composer (not a popover from the `+` button).

**Trigger detection:**
- Typing `/` anywhere in the input opens the dropdown sourced from `assistConfig` (only `enabled` entries).
- Typing `@` anywhere in the input opens the dropdown sourced from `toolsConfig` (only `enabled` entries).
- Detection must work mid-text, not just at the start of the input (scan from cursor position backward to the nearest whitespace/start-of-string to find the active token).

**Filtering:**
- As the user types more characters after `/` or `@`, filter the list live, case-insensitive, substring or prefix match against `id`/`label`, sorted alphabetically among matches.
- No matches → dropdown closes.

**Keyboard & mouse interaction:**
- `↓` / `↑` — move highlighted selection within the open list (wraps at ends).
- `Tab` — autocompletes the currently highlighted item's trigger text inline into the input (partial → full), keeping the dropdown open if there are still multiple candidates sharing that prefix, or closing it if the match is now unique.
- `Enter` or mouse click on an item — commits that selection fully (see §5 for what "commit" means per type) and closes the dropdown.
- `Space` right after a fully-typed, exact-match trigger also commits it and returns the caret to normal typing.
- `Esc` — closes the dropdown without committing, leaving typed text as-is.

**Positioning:** dropdown slides up, docked to the top edge of the composer, matching composer width or a reasonable max-width, scrollable if the list is long.

